# A loop header's global bytes per CTA over one run of the loop's own
# blocks: a store of 4 B by its one thread on each of 4 trips requests
# 16 B; its address reads the counter through `and.b32 %r2, %r1, 1`,
# which the analysis does not trace, so the distinct bytes and their
# sectors are not known.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/counter_mod_offset.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips 4 | global per CTA: requested 16 B, unique ? | warp * × lane * | exec 4/CTA{{$}}
